summary:
- topic: FY2026 Budget Process
  text: A special meeting was held to approve the FY2026 budget articles, a procedural
    step expedited to meet the City Council's schedule.
- topic: Personnel
  text: The Superintendent announced the resignations of Erica Matio (Director of
    Curriculum, Instruction, and Assessment), Samantha Matoya (SPHS Social Studies),
    and LB Murphy (SPHS Student Engagement Coordinator).
- topic: FY2026 Budget Approval
  text: The Superintendent read 19 budget action items for the FY2026 school budget,
    totaling $73,131,556, which were subsequently voted on by the board.
- topic: Budget Vote on Regular Instruction
  text: The board voted separately on budget article 3.1 for Regular Instruction,
    which passed 4-2. Two members voted in opposition to protest the lack of funding
    for social-emotional learning.
- topic: Budget Vote on Other Articles
  text: The board voted to group and unanimously approve the remaining 18 budget articles
    in two separate bloc votes for efficiency.
- topic: Capital Improvement Plan
  text: The approved budget articles included authorization for the FY26 School Department
    Capital Improvement Plan in the amount of $3,972,000.
- topic: Community Engagement
  text: The Superintendent promoted a community food drive taking place at the South
    Portland Police Department.
- topic: Next Steps
  text: The approved budget will be presented to the City Council for a vote on May
    6th, followed by a school budget referendum on June 10th.
